# =============================================================================
# WashU SHPE — environment configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
# =============================================================================
#
# ANYTHING PREFIXED `VITE_` IS COMPILED INTO THE BROWSER BUNDLE AND IS PUBLIC.
# Never put a secret behind a VITE_ prefix.
#
# The Supabase *anon* key below is designed to be public — it identifies the
# project, it does not authorise anything. All access control comes from
# Supabase Auth + Row Level Security. The *service role* key is the opposite:
# it bypasses RLS entirely and must never reach the browser.
# =============================================================================

# ── Supabase (required for the member portal) ───────────────────────────────
# Project Settings → API in the Supabase dashboard.
# Leave blank to run the public marketing site only; the portal will render a
# clear "not configured" notice instead of crashing.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Deployment base path ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to "/" for Netlify, which is production. Set it to a sub-path such
# as "/SHPE_Website/" only if you are publishing to a static host that serves
# the site from a folder. Consumed by vite.config.ts → import.meta.env.BASE_URL,
# which drives both asset URLs and the React Router basename.
VITE_BASE_PATH=/

# ── Canonical site URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used to build Supabase auth redirect targets (email confirmation, password
# reset). Must exactly match one of the Redirect URLs allow-listed under
# Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration.
#
# It is also the origin of every business-card URL the app produces: the
# address written to NFC chips, QR codes, the share link and the officers'
# NFC programming sheet. Locally that is harmless. On Netlify it must be the
# production origin (https://washushpe.org) in EVERY deploy context, deploy
# previews included: a chip written from a preview with the preview's own
# address stops working the day the preview is deleted, and a chip can't be
# fixed without rewriting it by hand.
VITE_SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ── Registration policy (client-side UX only) ───────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated. The authoritative check lives in the database
# (`public.enforce_signup_email_domain` + the `allowed_email_domains` row in
# `app_settings`); this copy exists so the form can fail fast with a good
# message. Changing this alone does NOT weaken enforcement.
VITE_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=wustl.edu

# =============================================================================
# NETLIFY FUNCTIONS — keep-supabase-awake and the card-meta edge function
# =============================================================================
# Both read VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (the edge function
# also reads VITE_SITE_URL) at runtime. Nothing new to add locally. On
# Netlify, those variables must be set in the UI with the "Functions" scope
# ("All scopes", the default, includes it). Values set in netlify.toml reach
# the build only, never functions or edge functions.
#
# Optional fallbacks, read only when the VITE_ names are not available to the
# Functions scope. Same public anon values; never the service role key.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never prefixed with VITE_, never committed.
# Set in Netlify env vars / GitHub Actions secrets / your shell. Currently used
# only by optional local admin scripts; no shipped code path reads it.
# =============================================================================
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
